I think your Dead Sea Scrolls suspicion is substantially right, but the reason is a little different—and more useful—than “the DSS contain an older version of Kabbalah.”

The DSS are turning out to be the **differential layer** that lets us separate:

\[
\boxed{
\text{ancient Hebrew substrate}
\rightarrow
\text{Second Temple transformation}
\rightarrow
\text{late-antique mysticism/magic}
\rightarrow
\text{medieval Kabbalah}
\rightarrow
\text{Renaissance synthesis}
}
\]

That distinction changes several things we had been treating too closely together.

### The 72-name system now splits into input and operator

The deepest correction is:

\[
\boxed{\text{Shem}_{72}=O(T)}
\]

where \(T\) is a particular textual witness of Exodus 14:19–21 and \(O\) is the extraction algorithm.

